      "body": "The 2026 MTN8 semi-finals have delivered a fascinating twist for South African football bettors. Orlando Pirates, affectionately known as the Bucs, have successfully avoided a clash with Mamelodi Sundowns, one of the Premier Soccer League's (PSL) most formidable sides. Instead, the Pirates will face Sekhukhune United in the semi-finals, while Sundowns take on Golden Arrows. This draw opens up fresh betting angles for South African punters keen to capitalise on the MTN8\u2019s high-stakes drama.\n\n### MTN8 Semi-Finals Fixtures: What South African Bettors Need to Know\n\nThe MTN8 semi-finals are scheduled to be played over two legs, with the first leg kicking off early September and the second leg concluding later that month. Orlando Pirates will host Sekhukhune United at Orlando Stadium, a venue where the Bucs have traditionally enjoyed strong support and results. Meanwhile, Mamelodi Sundowns will face Golden Arrows, a matchup that promises its own excitement but is separate from the Pirates\u2019 path.\n\nFor South African bettors, this means the chance to back the Pirates without the immediate threat of Sundowns, who have been dominant in recent seasons. Sekhukhune United, while competitive, are generally considered underdogs compared to the PSL giants. This dynamic creates an interesting betting market where the Bucs are favourites but not guaranteed winners, offering value for those who study form and odds carefully.\n\n### Betting Odds and Market Comparison in South Africa\n\nWhen it comes to placing bets on the MTN8 semi-finals, South African bettors have access to several trusted bookmakers licensed by local regulators such as the WCGRB, NGB, and ECGBB. Among the top options are Hollywoodbets and Supabets, both offering competitive odds and appealing bonuses tailored for the South African market.\n\nHere\u2019s a comparison of illustrative odds for the Orlando Pirates vs Sekhukhune United semi-final first leg:\n\n| Outcome               | Holly